# Sutram language pack: संस्कृतम् (Sanskrit, Devanagari)
# Format: <native word> <sanskrit keyword>
# Usage: sutram --lang sanskrit input.sm output.bin
#
# The core keywords are already Sanskrit, written in Latin transliteration.
# This pack is the same words in their own script — Devanagari — so a program
# can be written in Devanagari and still compile to the same native machine
# code. No new keyword is introduced; every line below is a script variant of
# an existing core keyword.

मुख्य mukhya
वित्ति vitti
अङ्क anka
यदि yadi
अन्यत्र anya
यावत् yavat
पुनरावर्तन chakra
प्रतियाति prati
प्रक्रिया prakriya
लिख likha
पूर्ण purna
शून्य shunya
सूत्र sutra
क्रम krama
उद्देश्य agrim
गुण guna
भावना bhavana
पङ्क्ति mala
सृजन ganana
निषेध abhava
रचना rachana
आयोजन yoj
परिग्रह satya
ग्रहण grahan
पर्यन्त tak
शब्द shabda
दशम dasham
कोश kosh
कुरु kuru
निष्क्रिय yantra
सङ्ख्या sankhya

# R65: Additional native Devanagari aliases for existing compiler builtins.
# No keyword ID or operator semantics changes. Total builtin aliases below: 18.
# A Sanskrit word maps to the already-recognised Latin builtin name.
लेख likh
लिखा likha
स्थगित sthagita
पाद pad
द्वारम् dvaram
पाठ paadh
बन्ध band
निर्मित nirmmita
शब्दम् shabda
पङ्क्तिदैर्घ्य pankti_len
कोशपुष् kosh_push
कोशपोप् kosh_pop
कोशदैर्घ्य kosh_len
कोशक्षमता kosh_cap
कोशशुद्धि kosh_clear
कोशरिक्त kosh_empty
कोशशिखर kosh_peek
कोशनिर्गम kosh_dequeue

# R66: exact abbreviations, NOT arbitrary prefix matching or terminators.
# U+0970 belongs to the alias spelling. Danda remains the terminator.
वि॰ vitti
लि॰ likha
प्र॰ prakriya
प॰ prati
कोशप्रवेश kosh_enqueue
